+- **The one exception: `backup-reader`, fleet-wide and read-only** (slice 022, an operator overrule of per-app-only). The S3 mirror (§"Backup") reads every production-stage bucket. A per-app user reads only its own buckets and can write them, so without the reader the mirror would hold every app's read-write key or the admin key; one reader, granted per bucket, reads them all and can change none. The prd `storage` release creates it with the provider's `homelab_s3_reader`: admin capability `buckets=read` (bucket enumeration through the admin API) and nothing more, `max_buckets = -1`, no bucket of its own. Its keys go into the Terraform-written Secret `backup-reader-credentials` in `storage-prd`. The grant is `homelab_s3_storage`'s `grant_backup_reader`: a bucket policy allowing the reader `s3:ListBucket` and `s3:GetObject`, and it is the bucket's whole policy. `terraform-modules/s3-storage` sets it for every namespace ending in `-prd`, so no call site sets anything and no new production bucket goes ungranted. The provider takes the reader's name from `HOMELAB_S3_BACKUP_READER`, set only in the prd cluster's env (HelmCharts `_providers/clusters.yaml`); on the dev cluster no reader is configured and the grant writes nothing.
 
